  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>This interesting catfish from Venezuela is offered only very rarely. With a maximum length of 10 cm (only very rarely do some specimens reach this size; the normal size is 6-7 cm) the species remains relatively small.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>It lives in the tributaries of the middle Orinoco in Venezuela.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>The flat body structure indicates that this species is adapted to stronger water currents. They should be offered temperatures in the range of 26-30°C, whereby one must pay attention to good oxygen saturation.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>They are typical Aufwuchs feeders.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>Pseudolithoxus species are all quite flat, but P. kelsorum especially. Besides the flat shape and appealing pattern, L189 has another characteristic that makes it particularly suitable for the aquarium: it is also very active during the day and by far not as addicted to hiding as many other L-catfish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>The sex differences are well pronounced at 5-6 cm length; the males can be recognized by the strong bristling (see photos).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudolithoxus-kelsorum-l189-2/",
      "html": "<p>No successful breeding of this species has been reported yet, but this is surely only due to the rare imports.</p>"
    }
  ],
